# shellcheck configuration for this repository.
#
# Scope: the two rules below are OPTIONAL checks -- they are off unless someone
# runs `shellcheck -o all`. They are disabled here so that an `-o all` run stays
# useful (signal, not 40 lines of noise) rather than being abandoned entirely.
# Every check enabled by default remains enabled; nothing real is suppressed.

# SC2250 -- "prefer ${var} over $var even when not required".
# Pure cosmetics: bash expands $repo and ${repo} identically, and the brace form
# only matters when a character that could continue the identifier follows.
# Honouring it would touch nearly every line of every script here to change no
# behaviour whatsoever. House style in this repo is bare $var, braces only where
# they disambiguate (${var}_suffix, ${arr[@]}, ${var:-default}).
disable=SC2250

# SC2312 -- "consider invoking this command separately to avoid masking its
# return value".
# The masking is deliberate wherever it appears here. `find ... 2>/dev/null |
# wc -l` must count zero for an unreadable directory rather than abort the
# caller; `stat ... || echo unknown` already handles its own failure. Obeying
# this rule would make the scripts MORE brittle at exactly the moments they are
# written to survive -- see scripts/.scripts/git-health.
disable=SC2312

# NOTE: shellcheck reads .shellcheckrc from the working directory, or from the
# checked file's directory walking upward. Stow-deployed scripts are covered:
# verified that `cd /tmp && shellcheck -o all ~/.scripts/git-health-boot` picks
# this file up, because the symlink resolves back into this repo before the
# upward walk. Bypass it with `shellcheck --norc` to see the raw output.
